Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: resolve the neighbour before a neigh xmit

Since commit b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path"),
the FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH path writes neigh->ha into the link-layer
header itself instead of passing the packet to neigh_xmit(). It never
looks at the neighbour state, so the state machine does not run for an
offloaded flow:

- A neighbour that is not resolved, such as one ip_neigh_gw4() has just
  created, has an all-zero address, and the packet leaves for
  00:00:00:00:00:00. A bridge floods it to every port.
- A neighbour whose host has left stays STALE, since nothing moves it
  to DELAY and PROBE, and the flow keeps sending to the old address for
  as long as the sender does. A bridge floods that once the fdb entry
  ages out.

Call neigh_event_send() as the classic output path does. It moves a
STALE neighbour to DELAY so that it is probed, and starts resolution for
one that is unresolved or failed. When the neighbour cannot be used yet,
tear the flow down and drop the packet, as for the other transmit
failures here. The classic path then queues later packets until
resolution completes.
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
@@ -469,7 +469,7 @@ nf_flow_offload_ip_hook(void *priv, stru
 			return NF_DROP;
 		}
 		neigh = ip_neigh_gw4(rt->dst.dev, rt_nexthop(rt, flow->tuplehash[!dir].tuple.src_v4.s_addr));
-		if (IS_ERR(neigh)) {
+		if (IS_ERR(neigh) || neigh_event_send(neigh, NULL)) {
 			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
 			return NF_DROP;
 		}
@@ -774,7 +774,7 @@ nf_flow_offload_ipv6_hook(void *priv, st
 			return NF_DROP;
 		}
 		neigh = ip_neigh_gw6(rt->dst.dev, rt6_nexthop(rt, &flow->tuplehash[!dir].tuple.src_v6));
-		if (IS_ERR(neigh)) {
+		if (IS_ERR(neigh) || neigh_event_send(neigh, NULL)) {
 			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
 			return NF_DROP;
 		}
